cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "peregrin: fast CPU simulation of large batches of small quantum circuits, with a PennyLane device"
authors:
  - family-names: Wolff
    given-names: Carson
repository-code: "https://github.com/carsonwolff/pennylane-peregrin"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  peregrin is a state-vector simulator for large batches of small (1 to 10 qubit) quantum
  circuits, built for quanvolutional preprocessing, where one circuit runs once per image
  patch. The core is written in Rust and runs a whole batch in one call. It is available
  from Python and as the PennyLane device peregrin.cpu.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum machine learning
  - quanvolution
  - PennyLane
  - simulator
